    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26860" root="طق" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَقْطَقَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَقْ</span>, in four places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  In the
language of the common people, it means <i>Lightness,</i> or <i>promptness, in speech.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And
(assumed tropical:)  The <i>death that results from the jinn's piercing</i>
or <i>thrusting</i> [i. e. <i>from the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَاعُون</span>]. (TA.)

